course: dictionary
lesson: 8954
title: Silvery and the picture it paints
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words paint a picture in the reader's mind. «Silvery» is one of them. It means shiny and grey-white, like silver. When you meet it, picture the thing being described and ask: what would it look like?
explain: Read this: «A whiting is a real silvery fish of the cod family from the North Sea.» The word silvery tells you the fish shines with a grey-white colour, like silver. You can use the same clue for water, moonlight, frost or metal.
explain: Silvery can also describe a sound or hair. A silvery sound is high, clear and pleasant, like a little bell. Silvery hair is grey or white and shining. The meaning changes a little, but the idea of something bright and light stays the same.
fact: «Silvery» means shiny and grey-white, like silver.
fact: A silvery sound is high, clear and pleasant, like a little bell.
fact: Silvery hair is grey or white and shining.
fact: «A whiting is a real silvery fish of the cod family from the North Sea.» Here silvery describes the fish's shine.
fact: Writers use silvery for moonlight, water, fish and frost to make a picture soft and beautiful.
exercise: «A whiting is a real silvery fish of the cod family from the North Sea.» What colour does silvery tell you the fish is? | *Shiny grey-white, like silver | Golden and warm | Bright red with spots | Dark green and very large
exercise: A silvery sound is high, clear and pleasant, like a little bell. Which thing does this sound remind you of? | *A little bell | A barking dog | A slammed door | A rumbling lorry
exercise: Find the word that means shiny grey-white, like silver. | heavy | *silvery | dull | crooked
test: «The moon made the lake look silvery.» What does silvery describe? | The lake's smell | *The shining, grey-white look of the lake | The sound of the water | The lake's depth and cold
test: Grandma's hair is silvery. What does this tell you about her hair? | It is wet and tangled | It is bright red | *It is grey or white and shining | It is very short
exam: Jayden reads «silvery moonlight» and says it means dark and gloomy. Which answer is right? | Silvery moonlight is warm and orange | Silvery moonlight is shiny grey-white light, like silver | Silvery moonlight is very loud | *Silvery moonlight is dark and gloomy, like a cloudy night
